\begin{array}{ll} r_0=7\\z_0=49\end{array}
The upper boundary of \mathcal{W} is the plane z=49, and the lower boundary is z={x}^2+{y}^2={r}^2. Therefore, {r}^2\le z\le 49.
The projection \mathcal{D} onto the xy-plane is the circle {x}^2+{y}^2=49 or r=7. That is, \mathcal{D}: \,0\le \theta \le 2\pi,\, 0\le r\le 7 The inequalities defining \mathcal{W} in cylindrical coordinates are thus \mathcal{W}: \,0\le \theta \le 2\pi,\, 0\le r\le 7,\, {r}^2\le z\le 49 Therefore, we obtain the following integral: \int\!\!\int\!\!\int _{\mathcal{W}} z \,dV= \int_0^{2\pi } \int_0^{7} \int_{{r}^2}^{49} zr \,dz \,dr \,d\theta= \int_0^{2\pi } \int_0^{7} \frac{{z}^2r}{2}\bigg|_{z={r}^2}^{49} \,dr\,d\theta=\int_0^{2\pi } \int_0^{7} \frac{r(2401-{r}^4)}{2} \,dr \,d\theta= \int_0^{2\pi } \int_0^{7} \frac{{2401}r-{r}^5}{2} \,dr \,d\theta= \int_0^{2\pi } \frac{2401 {r}^2}{4}-\frac{{r}^6}{12}\bigg|_0^{7} \,d\theta=19608.2\int_0^{2\pi } \,d\theta = 39216.3\pi
